{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Give same-sex couples equal access to NHS-funded IUI and IVF in England",
        "additional_details": "Opposite-sex couples are not asked to pay to prove their fertility. Same-sex couples are. IUI costs approx \u00a31,600 per cycle privately, and many ICBs require 6 to 12 self-funded IUI cycles before being offered NHS funded fertility treatment, despite the 2022 Women's Health Strategy pledge to end this. Some couples may pay up to \u00a325,000 before NHS help. We ask the Government to set a national standard so access no longer depends on sexuality or postcode. Make fertility care fair.",
        "background": "Many NHS areas in England make same-sex couples pay privately for 6 to 12 IUI cycles before NHS IVF, costing up to \u00a325,000. The Government pledged to end this in 2022. We want one national standard giving same-sex couples the same access to NHS-funded IUI and IVF as opposite-sex couples.",
